        <h3 class="cw__name">Embroidery</h3>
        <p class="cw__tags">Ahir · Suf · Paako</p>
        <p class="cw__copy">Each village of Kutch stitches its own signature: Suf counted from the reverse, Paako worked tight from the front, Aabhla caging a mirror in thread.</p>
        <a class="cw__piece" href="/products/beige-hand-mutwa-embroidered-kanchli-copy"><span class="cw__piece-t"><small>The piece</small><b>Red Hand Ahir Embroidered Kanchli</b></span><span class="cw__piece-p">Rs. 25,000</span><i class="sj-i sj-i--arrow-right ms" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      </article>
      <article class="cw__text" data-i="1">
        <p class="cw__no"><b>02</b> / 04</p>
        <h3 class="cw__name">Block print</h3>
        <p class="cw__tags">Hand block · Carved wood · Cotton</p>
        <p class="cw__copy">Cloth printed by hand with carved wooden blocks, the pattern laid down one press at a time along its length.</p>
        <a class="cw__piece" href="/products/dress-copy-2"><span class="cw__piece-t"><small>The piece</small><b>Modal Hand Block Printed Dress</b></span><span class="cw__piece-p">Rs. 3,500</span><i class="sj-i sj-i--arrow-right ms" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      </article>
      <article class="cw__text" data-i="2">
        <p class="cw__no"><b>03</b> / 04</p>
        <h3 class="cw__name">Tie-dye</h3>
        <p class="cw__tags">Shibori · Fold · Bind</p>
        <p class="cw__copy">Folded and bound by hand before the cloth meets the dye. The pale lines are where the binding kept the colour out.</p>
        <a class="cw__piece" href="/products/top-copy-14"><span class="cw__piece-t"><small>The piece</small><b>Shibori Mandarin Collar Top</b></span><span class="cw__piece-p">Rs. 4,200</span><i class="sj-i sj-i--arrow-right ms" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      </article>
      <article class="cw__text" data-i="3">
        <p class="cw__no"><b>04</b> / 04</p>
        <h3 class="cw__name">Weaving</h3>
        <p class="cw__tags">Handloom · Extra weft · Kutch</p>
        <p class="cw__copy">Woven on the handlooms of Kutch, its motifs picked into the cloth with an extra weft, as its weavers have done for generations.</p>
        <a class="cw__piece" href="/products/top-copy-9"><span class="cw__piece-t"><small>The piece</small><b>Handwoven Sleeveless Button-Front Top</b></span><span class="cw__piece-p">Rs. 3,360</span><i class="sj-i sj-i--arrow-right ms" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
      </article>
